                    {
                        "sense_id": "3024e3e0-763a-351d-a1b1-1cb3716ce03b",
                        "entry_id": "3b267b5f-c2fd-32ea-b843-53e4418b5dfd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative form of snipey.",
                            "Full of or attractive to snipe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "443f4cc5-9acd-42c1-bb52-28be4d403985",
                                "sense_id": "3024e3e0-763a-351d-a1b1-1cb3716ce03b",
                                "text": "The wind was blowing almost a storm as we arrived at our first ground -- a good-sized lake, with broad moory flats, sprinkled with bulrushes and sedgy grass stretching down to the water's edge, and looking uncommonly snipy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b40becb0-85bb-4744-8984-1636f3bd1986",
                                "sense_id": "3024e3e0-763a-351d-a1b1-1cb3716ce03b",
                                "text": "To all this I agreed, and having borrowed a gun from one of my Rifle Officer friends, and a good stock of ammunition, I joined my two new friends at funfire in the morning, and after driving about 6 miles, I saw some very snipy-looking fields, got down, my companions promising to call for me about 11 o'clock on their way back."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1da7fc6-dcc8-4624-893f-487ccff70657",
                                "sense_id": "3024e3e0-763a-351d-a1b1-1cb3716ce03b",
                                "text": "Some however, say it is the result of a capricious disposition which induces them to leave \"snipy places\" for other spots, but though possible, I am, after many years careful observation, inclined to disagree."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a1864c1f-0fbb-3b49-b260-e911e05c7142",
                        "entry_id": "3b267b5f-c2fd-32ea-b843-53e4418b5dfd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative form of snipey.",
                            "Long, narrow, and pointed."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d7e4fa0-fe59-4e91-811b-8af72840c222",
                                "sense_id": "a1864c1f-0fbb-3b49-b260-e911e05c7142",
                                "text": "The muzzle is strong and squared off, never snipy."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "25d5525d-e1de-3446-8c71-4a4dfdb55fd4",
                        "entry_id": "3b267b5f-c2fd-32ea-b843-53e4418b5dfd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative form of snipey.",
                            "Prone to sniping."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "013881f4-ceb4-452e-b2a7-e2ff2c8a0173",
                                "sense_id": "25d5525d-e1de-3446-8c71-4a4dfdb55fd4",
                                "text": "On 16 December 1878 Marian went to court to prove the will, an ordeal which even the usually snipy George Simpson though she should have been spared."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
